WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.175
Pension fund conflicts.

00:00:02.125 --> 00:00:04.636
Your retirement, their investments.

00:00:04.636 --> 00:00:15.386
Canada's major pension funds — CPPIB, PSP Investments, the Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan, and the Caisse de dépôt — collectively control over two trillion dollars in assets.

00:00:15.386 --> 00:00:21.590
These funds invest globally in infrastructure, real estate, healthcare, energy, and private equity.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.352
The government sets the policy environment that determines the value of these investments.

00:00:26.352 --> 00:00:30.704
Immigration policy affects housing demand and real estate values.

00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:34.340
Healthcare policy affects healthcare company valuations.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.636
Energy policy affects pipeline and renewable energy investments.

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:43.647
Climate policy affects the transition assets that Brookfield and similar firms manage.

00:00:43.647 --> 00:00:46.659
The pension funds are arm's-length from government.

00:00:46.659 --> 00:00:53.738
But the policy decisions that affect their returns are not arm's-length from the political leadership that emerged from the same financial ecosystem.

00:00:53.738 --> 00:00:57.545
Canada's major pension funds and their investment conflicts.

00:00:57.545 --> 00:00:59.715
The conflict architecture.

00:00:59.715 --> 00:01:04.215
Four intersections where pension fund investments conflict with public interest.

00:01:04.215 --> 00:01:06.261
The pension fund layer.

00:01:06.261 --> 00:01:09.715
Pension funds are not the cause of institutional capture.

00:01:09.715 --> 00:01:15.568
They are the mechanism that ensures every Canadian is financially invested in the system's continuation.

00:01:15.568 --> 00:01:21.659
When your retirement depends on rising property values, your financial interest opposes affordable housing.

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:27.681
When your pension invests in private healthcare, your financial interest aligns with public system degradation.

00:01:27.681 --> 00:01:35.715
When your retirement fund holds climate transition assets, your financial interest supports the policy framework created by the PM's former employer.

00:01:35.715 --> 00:01:43.318
This is the most sophisticated layer of the capture architecture: it makes every citizen a financial participant in the system that harms them.

00:01:43.318 --> 00:01:48.863
You cannot reform the system without threatening the retirement savings of the people who depend on the system.

00:01:48.863 --> 00:01:51.136
This is not a conspiracy.

00:01:51.136 --> 00:01:53.272
It is structural design.
